  "history": {
    "claims": [
      {
        "text": "In The Legends of Ren Zu, wisdom Gu teaches Ren Zu that the road of death into the Door of Life and Death is the road left behind by destiny Gu when it left fairness Gu, called the path of destiny. The road of life is the path destiny Gu treaded when it visited fairness Gu, also called the path of destiny.",
        "chapters": [
          410
        ],
        "certainty": "canon",
        "confidence": "B",
        "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
        "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
        "section": "intro",
        "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
        "mentions": [
          "sys_the_legends_of_ren_zu",
          "gu_wisdom_gu",
          "char_ren_zu",
          "loc_door_of_life_and_death",
          "gu_fairness_gu"
        ]
      },
      {
        "text": "Fairness Gu tells Ren Zu that both paths in the Door of Life and Death appeared because of destiny Gu, and that life and death are determined by destiny.",
        "chapters": [
          411
        ],
        "certainty": "canon",
        "confidence": "B",
        "verification": "citation_unchecked",
        "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
        "section": "intro",
        "text_origin": "source_excerpt"
      },
      {
        "text": "Fang Yuan notes that the text clearly indicated the existence of destiny Gu, and that the second generation Immortal Venerable of Heavenly Court, the creator of wisdom path, controlled this Gu and could plot against three future Demon Venerables. In three kings blessed land, the land spirit says Red Lotus Demon Venerable broke the restriction of destiny, allowing all life to regain control of their own fate.",
        "chapters": [
          546
        ],
        "certainty": "canon",
        "confidence": "B",
        "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
        "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
        "section": "early-lore-note",
        "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
        "mentions": [
          "char_fang_yuan",
          "fac_heavenly_court",
          "char_red_lotus_demon_venerable"
        ]
      },
      {
        "text": "Bing Sai Chuan explains that Heavenly Court can use fate Gu as an immortal material, refine it with a luck path Immortal Gu, and create destiny Gu. He says destiny Gu was first conceptualized by Giant Sun Immortal Venerable, that Heavenly Court wants rank ten destiny Gu in one go, and that Longevity Heaven only wants rank nine destiny Gu, so the fate Gu they use need not be fully restored. With rank nine destiny Gu, he claims Longevity Heaven could contest Heavenly Court and dominate the five regions.",
        "chapters": [
          1715
        ],
        "certainty": "canon",
        "confidence": "B",
        "verification": "citation_unchecked",
        "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
        "section": "longevity-heaven-plan",
        "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
        "mentions": [
          "char_bing_sai_chuan",
          "gu_fate_gu",
          "sys_immortal_gu",
          "char_giant_sun_immortal_venerable",
          "fac_longevity_heaven"
        ]
      },
      {
        "text": "Fairy Zi Wei knows Heavenly Court’s plan for destiny Gu, and that Longevity Heaven is also ambitious toward it. Heavenly Court had sought fortune rivalling heaven Immortal Gu, while Longevity Heaven seeks fate Gu, both aiming at destiny Gu.",
        "chapters": [
          1726
        ],
        "certainty": "canon",
        "confidence": "B",
        "verification": "citation_unchecked",
        "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
        "section": "longevity-heaven-plan",
        "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
        "mentions": [
          "char_fairy_zi_wei"
        ]
      }
    ]
  },
